/* voyager.claude-cjk-render-fix — even CJK rendering on macOS.
 * Two issues compound:
 * 1. Claude's CJK font stack lists Japanese/Traditional fonts (Hiragino,
 *    PingFang TC) before PingFang SC, so some Simplified characters
 *    (这/些/术/语…) get grabbed by them and render visibly thinner —
 *    the "some thin, some normal" effect.
 * 2. Body text is set to font-weight 360, a value CJK fallback fonts lack, so
 *    macOS synthesizes an uneven faux weight.
 * Fix: pull PingFang SC to the front of the CJK stack so Simplified text is
 * uniform, normalize plain body text to a real 400, and disable weight
 * synthesis. <strong> carries its own heavier weight, so bold stays bold. */
.standard-markdown :where(p, li, ul, ol, blockquote, dd, dt, td, th),
.font-claude-response-body {
  font-family: "Anthropic Serif", Georgia, "PingFang SC", "Hiragino Sans", "Microsoft YaHei", "Noto Sans CJK SC", sans-serif !important;
  font-weight: 400 !important;
  font-synthesis-weight: none !important;
}
